Imagine you are in a very big school with thousands of children in it. That school is China.

Now imagine that every single child in that school gets to send one grown-up to a special meeting room. All those grown-ups together are called the **National People's Congress**, or **NPC**.

Here is what they do:

1. **They make the rules.** Just like your class needs rules so everyone plays fairly, the whole country needs rules. The NPC makes the big rules that everyone follows.
2. **They pick the leaders.** They choose the people who help run the country, like the President and the Prime Minister.
3. **They check things.** They make sure the leaders are doing their jobs properly and that the country is doing well.

The most important thing to remember is this: **the people of China choose who goes to this meeting.** So the NPC is like the biggest classroom in the world, where the grown-ups talk about how to look after everyone.

It happens in Beijing, and it takes about two weeks every year. When it happens, people all over China watch it on television, just like you might watch a big school assembly! [end of text]


